{"study_accession":"PRJNA625305","secondary_study_accession":"SRP256366","title":"CD5 levels define functionally heterogeneous populations of naïve human CD4+ T cells","description":"Studies from mouse models show that differences in self-reactivity, as read-out by CD5 levels, identifies naïve T cell subsets with distinct functional properties during an immune response. Whether CD5 levels can also be used to parse functional biases in naive human CD4+ T cells is incompletely understood. Our study establishes CD5 as a reliable marker of T cell self-reactivity and functional heterogeneity in human CD4+ T cells. Overall design: Naïve CD4+ T cells from peripheral blood mononuclear cells of 2 human donors were sorted on top and bottom 15% of CD5 expression. (2 biological replicates; 4 conditions: CD5lo and CD5hi for each donor).","pubmed":"33682083","geo_series":"","n_samples":4,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN14596978","study_accession":"PRJNA625305","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"2_Hi","description":"2_Hi","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM4476324","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":4,"first_public":"2020-04-16","attributes":[["source_name","CD5hi"],["cell_type","Peripheral Blood Mononuclear Cells (PBMC)"],["cell_subtype","Naïve CD4+ T cells"],["sorting strategy","Sorted on top 15% of CD5 expression"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR11545310","experiment_accession":"SRX8115387","library_layout":"SINGLE","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"NextSeq 500","read_count":13021753,"base_count":1106849005,"first_public":"2020-04-16","experiment_title":"NextSeq 500 sequencing: GSM4476324: 2_Hi Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"},{"run_accession":"SRR11545311","experiment_accession":"SRX8115387","library_layout":"SINGLE","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"NextSeq 500","read_count":12692832,"base_count":1078890720,"first_public":"2020-04-16","experiment_title":"NextSeq 500 sequencing: GSM4476324: 2_Hi Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"},{"run_accession":"SRR11545312",